    <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 14px 0;">Hybrid is a <strong style="font-weight:700;">subset</strong> of structured. A system that produces structured output trivially generates hybrid output. The reverse is not true. By choosing hybrid, you're investing the same implementation budget — the same 10&#8211;16 weeks — for a format that delivers only 5&#8211;15% marginal straight-through processing improvement, cannot enable field-level sanctions screening, and <strong style="font-weight:700;">guarantees a second migration project</strong> when enforcement tightens after November 2026.</p>

    <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 20px 0;">Choose structured, and the same investment delivers <strong style="font-weight:700;">98%+ straight-through processing rates</strong>, 30% reduction in sanctions screening false positives, and full regulatory alignment — with no second project on the horizon.</p>

    <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 20px 0;">Same effort. Same timeline. Same cost. One gives you the floor. The other gives you the ceiling.</p>

