    <h2 style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-weight:900;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 20px 0;letter-spacing:-0.3px;">PMPG Updates: Hybrid Misuse Patterns Since Coexistence</h2>

    <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 14px 0;">Since SWIFT began MX/ISO 20022 coexistence in March 2023, the Payments Market Practice Group has been documenting a troubling pattern: institutions are treating hybrid addressing as the destination rather than the fallback.</p>

    <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 14px 0;">The specific misuse patterns emerging are ones regulators anticipated: institutions dumping entire unstructured addresses into a single free-text line without separately populating the required city and country fields. Others are using hybrid as a permanent state, with no roadmap to structured — despite three independent regulatory bodies converging on the same requirement.</p>

    <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 16px 0;">The convergence is worth repeating because it's rare:</p>

