            <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 10px 0;"><strong style="font-weight:700;">EPC</strong> mandates structured address elements for SEPA. City and country must be stored as separate, dedicated fields — not bundled into a single free-text line.</p>
            <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 10px 0;"><strong style="font-weight:700;">SWIFT CBPR+</strong> designates fully structured addressing as best practice, with hybrid treated as the minimum fallback only.</p>
            <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;color:#232F3E;margin:0;"><strong style="font-weight:700;">CPMI/BIS</strong> identifies structured address data as foundational to the G20 cross-border payments roadmap.</p>
